  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>kruskalwallis</keyword>
  <short_description>Kruskal-Wallis one-way analysis of variance by ranks.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>p = kruskalwallis(X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = kruskalwallis(X, group)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = kruskalwallis(X, group, displayopt)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[p, tbl, stats] = kruskalwallis(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>kruskalwallis</b> performs a nonparametric one-way analysis of variance by ranks. When <b>X</b> is a matrix and <b>group</b> is empty, columns are treated as groups. When <b>X</b> is a vector, <b>group</b> supplies one group label per observation.</p>
    <p><b>displayopt</b> can be <b>'on'</b> or <b>'off'</b>. <b>NaN</b> observations are omitted.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = [6 7 8; 5 7 9; 4 8 NaN; 6 9 10];
[p, tbl, stats] = kruskalwallis(X, [], 'off')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
